    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nLocated off the Navan Road, convenient to the Phoenix Park, Glenarriff Road is a pretty tree lined street of houses built in the 1960's. No.38 has been very well maintained over the years and will appeal to those seeking a family home with bright spacious accommodation, a central location, good gardens front and rear and a garage. \n\nThe accommodation comprises a large hallway with understairs storage leading to two spacious reception rooms both with parquet flooring and tiled fireplaces, the kitchen is fitted with a range of floor and wall units, upstairs there are three bedrooms, two generous sized doubles, both with fitted wardrobes and a single room. A family shower room completes the accommodation.\n\nTo the front there is off street parking while the south facing rear garden extends to approx. 12m and is laid in lawn with a selection of mature plants and shrubs and a useful garden shed for storage. There is the added benefit of a garage approx. 5m x 4.4m with access to a vehicular laneway.\n\nGlenarriff Road has long been regarded as a popular location for families being a short distance from the city centre and with easy access to the M50. Ashington Park and the Phoenix Park are both within a short walk and there are a wealth of shops and amenities on the doorstep with a large number of both national and secondary schools and sports clubs including St Oliver Plunkett GAA club. The property is also close to the great cafes and restaurants in Ashtown and just a short drive to Castleknock Village and Blanchardstown Shopping Centre."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 4m x 2m\nA porch leads to the spacious entrance hallway with wooden flooring and understairs storage.\n\nLiving Room - 3.8m x 3.4m\nThe living room to the front overlooks the tree lined road, features include parquet flooring and a tiled fireplace.\n\nDining Room - 4.1mx 3.8m\nAnother fine reception room with tiled fireplace, parquet flooring and views of the rear garden.\n\nKitchen - 3.2m x 2.2m\nFitted with a range of floor and wall units with space for a dining table.\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.1m x 3.4m\nLarge double bedroom with laminate flooring and an extensive range of fitted wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.4m x 3.4m\nAnother large double bedroom with a range of fitted wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.6m x 2.5m\nSingle room with laminate flooring.\n\nShower Room - 2.4m x 2.2m\nFully tiled shower room with w.c, wash hand basin and shower cubicle with Triton attachment.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Well maintained mid terrace 1960's built property</li><li>Pretty tree lined residential street</li><li>Many original features</li><li>Off street parking to the front and mature south facing rear garden</li><li>Garage to rear</li><li>Gas fired central heating</li><li>Large attic</li><li>Approx 15 minute walk to Ashtown train station</ul>"
      },
